<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>l8db</displayName>
  <description>Group Policy for l8db</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="l8db">l8db</string>
      <string id="Settings">Settings</string>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_l8db">l8db with Group Policy support</string>
      <string id="Organization">Organization</string>
      <string id="Organization_Help">The organization's name and an optional support note. Users see both in Settings under the organization policy.

Any l8db policy you set makes the app a managed installation; the name shows who manages it.

Disabled or Not Configured: no name.</string>
      <string id="AllowAi">Allow AI features</string>
      <string id="AllowAi_Help">The AI assistant and every AI call the app makes.

Disabled: blocked; the app rejects the related backend calls.

Enabled or Not Configured: allowed.</string>
      <string id="AllowExtensions">Allow extensions</string>
      <string id="AllowExtensions_Help">Community extensions and UI plugins.

Disabled: blocked; the app rejects the related backend calls.

Enabled or Not Configured: allowed.</string>
      <string id="AllowPersonalSync">Allow personal sync</string>
      <string id="AllowPersonalSync_Help">Syncing personal connections and settings.

Disabled: blocked; the app rejects the related backend calls.

Enabled or Not Configured: allowed.</string>
      <string id="AllowMcp">Allow MCP server</string>
      <string id="AllowMcp_Help">The MCP server for external AI clients, including "l8db mcp".

Disabled: blocked; the app rejects the related backend calls.

Enabled or Not Configured: allowed.</string>
      <string id="RequireSignedReleases">Require signed releases</string>
      <string id="RequireSignedReleases_Help">Production migrations run only from Git commits with a valid signature by one of the listed signers. Enter one fingerprint per line, as "git show --format=%GF" prints it. At least one signer is required.

The workstation needs the matching public keys, and for SSH signatures a trusted allowedSignersFile.

Disabled or Not Configured: no restriction.</string>
      <string id="Connections">Team connections (JSON)</string>
      <string id="Connections_Help">Connection profiles for every user on this computer, as a JSON array on one line like "connections" in policy.json; the box is single-line. Profiles add to the team file and win on matching IDs.

Do not enter passwords or other credentials: every user on this computer can read the value.

The box holds at most 32,767 characters. For more profiles, use the "Policy" registry value or the policy.json file.

Disabled or Not Configured: no profiles.</string>
      <string id="ProductionReadOnly">Open production read-only</string>
      <string id="ProductionReadOnly_Help">Production connections open read-only by default.

Enabled: turned on. Disabled: turned off. Either way, users cannot change the setting.

Not Configured: users decide.</string>
      <string id="ProductionConfirmCommit">Confirm commits on production</string>
      <string id="ProductionConfirmCommit_Help">The app asks before every commit on a production connection.

Enabled: turned on. Disabled: turned off. Either way, users cannot change the setting.

Not Configured: users decide.</string>
      <string id="ProductionAutoRollback">Roll back open production transactions</string>
      <string id="ProductionAutoRollback_Help">Open transactions on production connections are rolled back automatically.

Enabled: turned on. Disabled: turned off. Either way, users cannot change the setting.

Not Configured: users decide.</string>
      <string id="ConfirmDestructiveQueries">Guard destructive queries</string>
      <string id="ConfirmDestructiveQueries_Help">The app asks before DELETE, DROP, TRUNCATE and similar statements.

Enabled: turned on. Disabled: turned off. Either way, users cannot change the setting.

Not Configured: users decide.</string>
      <string id="SshTrustNewHosts">Accept new SSH host keys</string>
      <string id="SshTrustNewHosts_Help">Unknown SSH host keys are saved without asking. Keep this off on managed workstations.

Enabled: turned on. Disabled: turned off. Either way, users cannot change the setting.

Not Configured: users decide.</string>
      <string id="CrashReports">Send crash reports</string>
      <string id="CrashReports_Help">The app sends crash reports.

Enabled: turned on. Disabled: turned off. Either way, users cannot change the setting.

Not Configured: users decide.</string>
      <string id="UsageMetrics">Send usage and performance data</string>
      <string id="UsageMetrics_Help">The app sends usage and performance data.

Enabled: turned on. Disabled: turned off. Either way, users cannot change the setting.

Not Configured: users decide.</string>
      <string id="AutoUpdateCheck">Check for updates automatically</string>
      <string id="AutoUpdateCheck_Help">The app checks for new versions on its own. Turn off when software distribution delivers updates.

Enabled: turned on. Disabled: turned off. Either way, users cannot change the setting.

Not Configured: users decide.</string>
      <string id="AutoUpdateInstall">Install updates automatically</string>
      <string id="AutoUpdateInstall_Help">Updates that are found install without asking.

Enabled: turned on. Disabled: turned off. Either way, users cannot change the setting.

Not Configured: users decide.</string>
      <string id="SslDefaultMode">Default SSL mode</string>
      <string id="SslDefaultMode_Help">The SSL mode new connections are created with. Users cannot change it.

Disabled or Not Configured: users decide.</string>
      <string id="UpdateChannel">Update channel</string>
      <string id="UpdateChannel_Help">The channel the app gets updates from. Users cannot change it.

Disabled or Not Configured: users decide.</string>
      <string id="SslDefaultMode_Disable">No SSL (disable)</string>
      <string id="SslDefaultMode_Prefer">Prefer SSL (prefer)</string>
      <string id="SslDefaultMode_Require">Require SSL (require)</string>
      <string id="SslDefaultMode_VerifyCa">Verify certificate authority (verify-ca)</string>
      <string id="SslDefaultMode_VerifyFull">Verify certificate and host name (verify-full)</string>
      <string id="UpdateChannel_Stable">Stable</string>
      <string id="UpdateChannel_Canary">Canary</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="Organization">
        <textBox refId="Organization"><label>Organization name</label></textBox>
        <textBox refId="Support"><label>Support note (optional)</label></textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="RequireSignedReleases">
        <listBox refId="TrustedReleaseSigners">Approved signers</listBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="Connections">
        <textBox refId="Connections"><label>Connections as a JSON array on one line</label></textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="SslDefaultMode">
        <dropdownList refId="SslDefaultMode" noSort="true" defaultItem="4">SSL mode</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="UpdateChannel">
        <dropdownList refId="UpdateChannel" noSort="true" defaultItem="0">Channel</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
